# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf decides per machine what a checkout produces, so a
# Windows checkout writes CRLF while gofmt insists on LF. That makes gofmt -l . a
# false failure on every Go file the setting touched, and leaves files that git
# reports as modified while their content is identical.
#
# eol=lf keeps the working tree byte-identical across platforms, which is what
# the gofmt gate and the golden files in tests expect.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats must never be normalized; a rewritten line ending corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
*.db binary
*.db-wal binary
*.db-shm binary
*.bak binary

# Download archives and database files are produced at runtime, never edited.
*.sqlite binary
